            <ArticleTitle>Spread of Chikungunya Virus East/Central/South African Genotype in Northeast Brazil.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1742-1744</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3201/eid2310.170307</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We investigated an outbreak of exanthematous illness in Maceió by using molecular surveillance; 76% of samples tested positive for chikungunya virus. Genetic analysis of 23 newly generated genomes identified the East/Central/South African genotype, suggesting that this lineage has persisted since mid-2014 in Brazil and may spread in the Americas and beyond.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
